Body:
Hit the same symptom from a different angle — a non-TUI client (a custom desktop app built on `@opencode-ai/sdk`, subscribing to `session.diff` server events to drive its own UI) also never receives real diff data during normal turns, only on `/undo`. Tracing it down, I don't think TUI-side wiring alone will fix this even once implemented — the server-side event payload itself is empty for the code path this issue is about.

**Root cause**, still present on `main` as of this comment:

`packages/opencode/src/session/summary.ts`'s `summarize()` publishes `Session.Event.Diff` unconditionally with an **empty** payload, before ever computing the real diff:

```ts
const summarize = Effect.fn("SessionSummary.summarize")(function* (input: {
  sessionID: SessionID
  messageID: MessageID
}) {
  yield* sessions.setSummary({ sessionID: input.sessionID, summary: { additions: 0, deletions: 0, files: 0 } })
  yield* events.publish(Session.Event.Diff, { sessionID: input.sessionID, diff: [] })   // <-- always []
  if ((yield* config.get()).snapshot === false) return
  const all = yield* sessions.messages({ sessionID: input.sessionID }).pipe(Effect.orDie)
  if (!all.length) return

  const messages = all.filter(/* ... */)
  const target = messages.find((m) => m.info.id === input.messageID)
  if (!target || target.info.role !== "user") return
  const msgDiffs = yield* computeDiff({ messages })
  target.info.summary = { ...target.info.summary, diffs: msgDiffs }
  yield* sessions.updateMessage(target.info)   // real diffs land in message.summary.diffs...
  // ...but no second events.publish(Session.Event.Diff, ...) ever fires with msgDiffs.
})
```

The real computed diffs (`msgDiffs`) get written into `message.summary.diffs` via `updateMessage`, but `summarize()` never republishes the `Session.Event.Diff` event with that data — the one publish it does is the empty placeholder from the top of the function, before `msgDiffs` even exists.

Compare `packages/opencode/src/session/revert.ts`, which is the *only* place that publishes a real payload:

```ts
const diffs = yield* summary.computeDiff({ messages: range })
yield* storage.write(["session_diff", input.sessionID], diffs).pipe(Effect.ignore)
yield* events.publish(Session.Event.Diff, { sessionID: input.sessionID, diff: diffs })
```

So `session.diff` events carry real data only on `/undo`, never during ordinary editing — which matches this issue's own repro exactly ("revert dock renders... but no file rows" vs. the normal-turn sidebar never populating at all).

Practical implication for the fix: even if TUI-side wiring is added to consume `session_diff`/the event per this issue's "Decision needed" section, the sidebar will still render empty during normal edits, because the server never sends anything but `[]` for that path. A minimal server-side fix would be publishing the real `msgDiffs` after `computeDiff` resolves (either replacing the premature `diff: []` publish, or adding a second publish after `updateMessage`) — e.g.:

```ts
const msgDiffs = yield* computeDiff({ messages })
target.info.summary = { ...target.info.summary, diffs: msgDiffs }
yield* sessions.updateMessage(target.info)
yield* events.publish(Session.Event.Diff, { sessionID: input.sessionID, diff: msgDiffs })
```

Happy to open this as its own issue instead if you'd rather track the client-wiring and server-payload problems separately — flagging here first since they look like the same root cause to me.
